### Extraction Engine

Relevant module:

- `flow_extract.py`

Core behavior observed in code:

- Validates the trace before extraction.
- Computes screen hashes and field layout hashes.
- Builds transitions from screen-action-screen sequences.
- Extracts request fields from action inputs.
- Extracts response fields from final/output screens.
- Uses field-map metadata where available.
- Flags blockers when no input fields or no final output fields are found.
- Produces deterministic warning/blocker lists.
- Produces a replay case.
- Produces a flow graph.
- Computes confidence from blockers, warnings, plain-text-only state, and field confidence.

Business implication: this is the central core-technology component. Its value is not the pretty report; it is the deterministic conversion of noisy recorded screen behavior into a reviewable transaction model with confidence, hashes, fields, transitions, and replay evidence.

